llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: ReassociateOps keeps 3.8's operand order (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for an add (or another associative
operation) of a value and an operation with a constant. Upstream r262148
(982224cfb8de, 2016-02-27, "DAGCombiner: Don't unnecessarily swap
operands in ReassociateOps"), first released in 3.9.0, builds
(op y, (op x, c1)) as (op (op y, x), c1); 3.8 built (op (op x, y), c1).
The address of a member-function pointer's vtable slot shows it: the
game region loads it as `-0x1(%rcx,%rdx)`, the pointer's offset as base
and the vtable as index, at 49 sites, and in the other order at none
(rounds 138B and 145B). With this patch 0xd332b0 compiles to the base's
bytes and no matched game row changes (one function of the game module
changes: that draft).

--- a/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp	2026-11-11 04:02:54.832531182 +0000
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp	2026-11-11 04:02:54.841097078 +0000
@@ -880,9 +880,9 @@
         return SDValue();
       }
       if (N1.hasOneUse()) {
-        // reassoc. (op x, (op y, c1)) -> (op (op x, y), c1) iff x+c1 has one
-        // use
-        SDValue OpNode = DAG.getNode(Opc, SDLoc(N0), VT, N0, N1.getOperand(0));
+        // reassoc. (op y, (op x, c1)) -> (op (op x, y), c1) iff x+c1 has one
+        // use (PS4: LLVM 3.8's operand order, before r262148)
+        SDValue OpNode = DAG.getNode(Opc, SDLoc(N0), VT, N1.getOperand(0), N0);
         if (!OpNode.getNode())
           return SDValue();
         AddToWorklist(OpNode.getNode());
